        "contact": {
          "url": "https://filmapi.vercel.app/"
        },
        "description": "Provides detailed information on various photo camera films in 35mm and 120 formats including brand name, film model, ISO, availability in different formats, black & white or color specification, processing type, image, film description, and key features.",
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "Production server",
            "url": "https://filmapi.vercel.app"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Film API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Browse a catalogue of 35mm and 120 photographic films with brand, ISO, colour/B&W and processing details",
        "homepage": "https://filmapi.vercel.app",
        "docs_url": "https://filmapi.vercel.app",
        "license_short": "No licence specified by the provider.",
        "license_md": "- The provider publishes no explicit licence or terms of use.\n- Treat film names, brand names, and product imagery as the property of their respective manufacturers.\n- Confirm acceptable use with the provider before relying on the data commercially.",
        "about_md": "The Film API is a small community catalogue of photographic still films, served from [filmapi.vercel.app](https://filmapi.vercel.app). It focuses on analogue stocks for 35mm and 120 (medium format) cameras.\n\nWhat you get from the API:\n\n- Film brand and product name\n- ISO (film speed) rating\n- Format availability flags for 35mm and 120\n- Colour vs black-and-white designation\n- Processing type (for example `c-41`, `e-6`, `b&w`)\n- A product image URL plus descriptive text and key feature notes\n\nThe service exposes a single REST endpoint, `GET /api/films`, which returns the full catalogue as a JSON array. No authentication is documented. CORS is reported as disabled, so calls from a browser will typically need a server-side proxy.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "film": "A photographic still film stock, listed with brand, name, ISO, format flags, colour/B&W, and processing details; the catalogue is returned by `GET /api/films`."
        },
